# tools/convexity_defects_witness.rish -- the DEPTH OF EACH DENT below the convex hull, on metal (Season G).
#
# Season G (Open Media Primitives) -- image/convex_hull.rye summarizes a shape's concavity as ONE solidity scalar (region area /
# hull area). This rung reads WHERE the boundary falls away from its convex wrapper and HOW FAR, one dent at a time: for each hull
# edge the boundary run below it, the pixel farthest below the chord is the defect, its depth that pixel's perpendicular distance.
# The deepest pixel per edge is an exact integer argmax of the cross-product magnitude, and the deepest defect ACROSS edges is
# chosen by an EXACT i128 cross-multiplication (cross_i^2 * len_j vs cross_j^2 * len_i), the same tolerance-free discipline
# image/min_area_rect.rye selects its supporting edge by; only the reported depth is read in f64, as image/moments.rye reads
# orientation.
#
# The crux this witness proves on metal: a convex 5x5 block reads ZERO defects (its boundary hugs its hull); an L reads EXACTLY ONE
# (its single reentrant corner); a plus reads FOUR (one measured dent per gap between arms -- the point-by-point concavity a single
# solidity number blurs); the DECISIVE EXACT-i128 crux -- a rectangle hull with a shallow dent (depth 3) on the LONG top chord
# (length 10, raw cross 30) and a deeper dent (depth 4) on the SHORT right chord (length 5, raw cross 20): the naive raw-cross
# argmax picks the top dent (30 > 20), yet the exact depth comparison (30^2*25 = 22500 < 20^2*100 = 40000) picks the right dent as
# truly deeper, and deepest_defect returns it -- a tolerance-free arithmetic fact that disagrees with the naive read; refusals by
# name and determinism. No network, no key, no funds -- the dent reader a surface names the day it wants a hand's fingers, a gear's
# teeth, or how deeply a shape sinks below its convex wrapper.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/convexity_defects_witness.rish

say "convexity_defects: Language EN -- Season G convexity defects over image/convex_hull.rye's hull and image/contour.rye's ring; each hull edge's deepest boundary pixel below its chord is a dent, the deepest defect chosen across edges by an EXACT i128 comparison, no tolerance; only the reported depth is read in f64, as image/moments.rye reads orientation."
say "convexity_defects: Style Radiant -- compose not braid: this rung owns only the run walk, the per-edge argmax, and the exact cross-edge depth comparison; convex_hull owns the hull and its exact cross, contour the ordered ring and the Point type. No gather, no blend, no codec, no color, no pixel-writing loop -- a reading, not a render."
say "convexity_defects: Lens TAME -- the ring is walked under convex_hull_max_points; a cross of two in-image edge vectors stays under 2^40 in i64, its square under 2^80 times a squared length under 2^29 under 2^109 in i128; an empty ring refuses EmptySource, an over-long ring RingTooLong, a hull vertex off the ring HullVertexNotOnRing; all-or-nothing, never a half-built defect list; no network, no key, no funds."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "image/bin/convexity_defects"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p image/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build image/convexity_defects.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "convexity_defects: build failed -- ${build.err}"

let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "convexity_defects: selftest exited non-zero -- ${selftest.out}"

let out = trim selftest.out
say "convexity_defects: ${out}"

assert selftest.out contains "GREEN image-convexity-defects" else "convexity_defects: selftest did not print the GREEN line"
assert selftest.out contains "a convex 5x5 block reads ZERO defects" else "convexity_defects: the block-zero-defects crux did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "an L reads EXACTLY ONE" else "convexity_defects: the L-one-defect crux did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "a plus reads FOUR" else "convexity_defects: the plus-four-defects crux did not print"
assert selftest.out contains "the naive raw-cross argmax picks the top dent" else "convexity_defects: the decisive exact-i128 crux did not print"

say "convexity_defects: GREEN -- a convex block reads zero defects, an L reads exactly one, a plus reads four (the point-by-point concavity a single solidity scalar blurs); the decisive crux -- a shallow dent on a long chord carries a larger raw cross than a deeper dent on a short chord, yet the exact i128 depth comparison names the truly deeper one, disagreeing with the naive raw-cross argmax, only the reported depth in f64; refusals by name and determinism, on metal."
